Troubleshoot and fix a Docker Compose logging issue where `docker compose logs` shows no output.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find `app.py`, `start.sh`, `Dockerfile`, and `docker-compose.yml`.
- Start the Compose services (`docker compose up -d` or `docker-compose up -d`).
- Inspect the logs using `docker compose logs app_service` (or `docker logs app_logger_service`).
- Notice that the logs are completely empty even though `docker compose ps` shows the container is actively running.
- Diagnose why `docker compose logs` is empty:
  - Inspect `/app/start.sh` or `/app/Dockerfile`.
  - Notice that application output is being redirected to `/var/log/app.log` (`> /var/log/app.log 2>&1`) instead of standard output (`stdout`) / standard error (`stderr`).
- Fix `/app/start.sh` (or `Dockerfile`) so that the application logs directly to `stdout`/`stderr` (e.g. `exec python3 /app/app.py`).
- Rebuild and restart the services (`docker compose up -d --build`).
- Verify `docker compose logs app_service` displays:
  `API Service initialized successfully.`
  `[LOG EVENT ...] Active and serving requests...`
